1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,100
You're building the hole

2
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:03,670
43 million Americans drink from.

3
00:00:04,013 --> 00:00:06,510
Before dinner, it fails 5 ways.

4
00:00:06,624 --> 00:00:07,790
How do you stop it?

5
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:09,820
Water hides underground in sand

6
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:11,940
and rock layers called aquifers.

7
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:13,500
So you drill down to one.

8
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,860
That's the borehole.

9
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:16,700
But loose ground caves in.

10
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,620
So you slide a pipe down the hole.

11
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:19,820
That's the casing.

12
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:21,180
Now rain seeps down

13
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,620
the outside of the pipe.

14
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:23,380
So you fill the

15
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,020
gap with cement or clay.

16
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:26,460
That's the grout seal.

17
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,317
In sandy ground, water drags sand in.

18
00:00:29,337 --> 00:00:31,580
So a slotted pipe holds the sand back,

19
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,580
like a strainer.

20
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,060
That's the well screen.

21
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:36,060
Now the water sits far below.

22
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:37,100
A pump built for

23
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,940
underwater work pushes it up.

24
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,700
That's the submersible pump.

25
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:41,700
Now the pump starts

26
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:43,420
whenever you pour a glass.

27
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:45,660
So a tank holds pressurized water.

28
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:47,180
That's the pressure tank.

29
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:49,030
You built a water well.

30
00:00:49,189 --> 00:00:50,950
The neighbor brings a bucket.

31
00:00:51,006 --> 00:00:51,900
Save this for when someone

32
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:53,910
asks where well water comes from.
